// Tail-recursive: the recursive call is the LAST operation
public static long factorialTail(int n, long acc) {
    if (n <= 1) return acc;
    return factorialTail(n - 1, n * acc);   // nothing pending after this
}
// In Scala/Kotlin @tailrec this is O(1) stack; in Java it is still O(n)
// and throws StackOverflowError around n=10,000.
```

